g Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $134K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["First Industrial Realty Trust,  is a mid-cap real estate business with a $7.6B market cap on $727M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 152% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5208000910976598},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DISTINKT, EINE NEUE, IN KALIFORNIEN LIZENZIERTE TALENTAGENTUR, BERBRINGT DIE BARSTANGEN FR DIE PROFESSIONELLE VERTRETUNG MIT EINEM NEUEN MODELL FR GLOBALES TALENT","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/distinkt-eine-neue-in-kalifornien-lizenzierte-talentagentur-uberbringt-die-barstangen-fur-die-professionelle-vertretung-mit-einem-neuen-modell-fur-globales-talent-302938201.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794506400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.892,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Financial Survey: One Liberty Properties (NYSE:OLP) versus First Industrial Realty Trust (NYSE:FR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/financial-survey-one-liberty-properties-nyseolp-versus-first-industrial-realty-trust-nysefr.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794417300.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.974,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the FR Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/new